From 651ac1109320fc2a6ab7d21c6cbb18880ca52214 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tomaz Zaman <tomaz@mono.si>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 03:59:10 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] mlan: revalidate the ralist after the send helpers drop
 the lock

wlan_dequeue_tx_packet() receives ptr from wlan_wmm_get_next_priolist_ptr()
with ra_list_spinlock held and passes it to wlan_11n_aggregate_pkt() or
wlan_send_single_packet(), both of which release the lock around the
host write and return with it released. It then reads ptr->sta and
ptr->sta->ps_sleep without the lock.

wlan_wmm_delete_peer_ralist() -- hostapd's del_station, through
woal_deauth_station() -- frees the ralist and its sta table under that
same lock, so a station leaving while its queue is being drained is a
use-after-free of a 96-byte raListTbl. KASAN, on an AP with one client
under a UDP flood that made hostapd deauthenticate it:

  BUG: KASAN: slab-use-after-free in wlan_wmm_process_tx+0x1fb4 [mlan]
  Read of size 8 at addr ffff00080c9ee2c8 by task kworker/u17:0/324
  Freed by task 242: wlan_wmm_delete_peer_ralist <- wlan_ops_uap_ioctl
    <- woal_deauth_station <- woal_cfg80211_del_station

The read is offset 72 of the ralist: ptr->sta.

Take the lock again, confirm the ralist is still on its tid list with
wlan_is_ralist_valid() -- the same check the senders make after they
re-lock -- and copy the address out before calling
wlan_update_ralist_tx_pause(), which takes the lock itself.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 mlan/mlan_wmm.c | 23 +++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mlan/mlan_wmm.c b/mlan/mlan_wmm.c
index 52c6e8a..ba00509 100644
--- a/mlan/mlan_wmm.c
+++ b/mlan/mlan_wmm.c
@@ -1955,8 +1955,27 @@ static int wlan_dequeue_tx_packet(pmlan_adapter pmadapter)
 		}
 	}
 
-	if (ptr->sta && ptr->sta->ps_sleep) {
-		wlan_update_ralist_tx_pause(priv, ptr->ra, 1);
+	/* The send helpers above return with ra_list_spinlock released, and
+	 * wlan_wmm_delete_peer_ralist() frees both the ralist and its sta
+	 * table under that lock. Re-validate ptr before reading it again and
+	 * copy out what is needed: wlan_update_ralist_tx_pause() takes the
+	 * lock itself, so it cannot be called while holding it.
+	 */
+	{
+		t_u8 ps_sleep = MFALSE;
+
+		pmadapter->callbacks.moal_spin_lock(pmadapter->pmoal_handle,
+						    priv->wmm.ra_list_spinlock);
+		if (wlan_is_ralist_valid(priv, ptr, ptrindex) && ptr->sta &&
+		    ptr->sta->ps_sleep) {
+			memcpy_ext(pmadapter, ra, ptr->ra, MLAN_MAC_ADDR_LENGTH,
+				   MLAN_MAC_ADDR_LENGTH);
+			ps_sleep = MTRUE;
+		}
+		pmadapter->callbacks.moal_spin_unlock(pmadapter->pmoal_handle,
+						      priv->wmm.ra_list_spinlock);
+		if (ps_sleep)
+			wlan_update_ralist_tx_pause(priv, ra, 1);
 	}
 
 	LEAVE();
